{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>A dull white spot.</b> Their white is not strong but dull." "<b>Bright spot.</b> Like the whiteness seen in the flesh of a ruddy person — called רוש\"ו — between the freckles of his redness; it is called בֹהַק, like a lentil-eater, in whom between one lentil and the next the flesh shines with a bright white."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "The la'az רוש\"ו is Old French rosé, 'rosy/red'; 'lentil-eater' renders אִישׁ עַדְשָׁן literally."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:15.354786463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}